SPDX declarations identify the applicable licence and copyright notices.
Files that cannot carry comments have adjacent plain-text .license files
with the same SPDX notices, following the REUSE standard. These project
declarations do not replace existing upstream terms or attribution; patch
context remains the work of its original authors. Standard licence templates
may contain copyright placeholders; the actual notices accompany each file.

Downloaded components and their notices keep their own licences.
NOTICE points to their licences and the matching source download.
Packages inside the Guix image also retain their own terms. A component's
source obligations are not satisfied merely by listing its licence or
upstream URL.

Our standards for readable, maintainable contributions are described in
docs/philosophy.md. They guide project review and add no restrictions to
the rights granted by these licences.
